// A forward/extern type declaration shares its shape with a nested definition and
// is separated from it only by the absence of a binding. The reference states
// that "@co.dap.declare is optional" for functions and types, so BOTH spellings
// are members here — the corpus previously carried only the annotated one, which
// let the physical-nesting guard reject the bare form unnoticed.
_ co.lang.class = {

    @co.dap.declare(extern)
    Dept co.lang.struct;

    Region co.lang.struct;

    getDept()->(Dept) = { }
}
